{"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"Cliques"}],"role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"fileName":"MaximalCliques.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques.swift#L259"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MaximalCliques"}],"title":"MaximalCliques","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:7Cliques07MaximalA0V"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every maximal clique of an undirected graph’s simple graph once, lazily, each in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order (by vertex index): an isolated vertex, or one whose only edges are loops, is a clique of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one. The order is Eppstein–Löffler–Strash’s: by the cliques’ first vertex in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering"},{"type":"text","text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"degeneracy d."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Cliques\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Cliques\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Cliques\/ST"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques"]]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Structures","title":